# Design paths this repository owns, matched against the SOFT half only.
#
# The CuBox fleet's fixed mount points. They appear verbatim in the captured
# fixtures, in the checks' own evidence and detail strings, and therefore in the
# parity baseline (tests/fixtures/parity-baseline.json) that records the real
# verdicts. One mount point per line, nothing broader. Credentials, HARD
# findings and the ENVFILE/KEYFILE checks are never allowlisted by this file.
/mnt/state
/mnt/recordings
/mnt/transcoded
/mnt/shared

# The two host paths .env.example names as the OPERATOR'S starting values. They
# are deployment values (a NAS volume layout), not credentials, and they cannot
# carry a trailing directive: `deploy.sh` and Docker's env-file parser read the
# whole right-hand side, so the directive would become part of the value.
/share/CACHEDEV1_DATA/Programs/sentinel/data
/share/CACHEDEV1_DATA/Programs/pvr
